 that surely works  well i've got you fans coming back into  stadiums this weekend  gonna see some fans back at premier  league matches  um but of course in tier three areas  there won't be any fans allowed back in  including of course for the manchester  clubs as well  it feels like a bit of a postcode  lottery do you think it's going to put  some clubs at a disadvantage  i don't believe personally it is um i  think that i'm happy to see fans come  back into stadiums  i do think this idea that salford city  if they were to come into theater in two  weeks can have 2 000 but manchester  united got 75 000 stadium  can have 2 000 is just madness i mean  surely manchester united can house more  than 2 000 people safely and socially  distance  at salford we might only be able to hold  1 200.  so again it's this blanket approach this  lack of bespoke  um approach to sort of different  situations  how do we deal with the hospitality  sector how do we deal with hospitality  do we want to close it we believe it  potentially causes health damage to us  okay we need a bespoke package for the  hospitality sector the travel sectors  that we know because we're putting  border restrictions in place we're not  allowing people to fly  okay this is the travel sector we're  gonna put up this boat package in place  it just seems to me to be a blanket  approach to everyone irrespective of the  good or the bad situation that you're in  and that's the same with football clubs  2 000 in a 10 000 stadium a 75 000  stadium or a 5 000 stadium  i'm happy about it it's the start you  know i know that we'll  they'll increase but it's the beginning  and we should be happy about it but  again it's just another  example of where you feel it's just a  case it's a bit lazy  it's a little bit lazy it's not really  leadership it's it's a goal just let  2000 back in where's the science behind  that  they always said they would look at the  science where is the science behind 2000  there can't be there can't be any  science thanks very much been really  fascinating to talk thank you

